71
00:06:40,660 --> 00:06:42,100
[The Story Untold]

72
00:06:42,100 --> 00:06:44,740
[Based on Twentine's novel "The Story Untold" on jjwxc.net]

73
00:06:44,980 --> 00:06:47,860
[Episode 4]

74
00:07:09,240 --> 00:07:09,850
What...

75
00:07:10,070 --> 00:07:11,190
What's going on?

76
00:07:17,870 --> 00:07:19,980
I couldn't reach the tenant downstairs.

77
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:21,330
I'll take you inside to have a look.

78
00:07:23,630 --> 00:07:24,180
See?

79
00:07:24,560 --> 00:07:25,000
Right there.

80
00:07:25,950 --> 00:07:26,490
Look.

81
00:07:26,950 --> 00:07:28,140
There's a leak coming from your place.

82
00:07:28,480 --> 00:07:30,370
It's soaked his entire ceiling.

83
00:07:31,270 --> 00:07:32,670
It's all over the apartment.

84
00:07:34,190 --> 00:07:36,290
I'll give him your contact information later.

85
00:07:36,830 --> 00:07:38,370
If there's any property damage,

86
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:39,780
he'll contact you directly.

87
00:07:42,360 --> 00:07:43,850
The damage is pretty bad.

88
00:07:44,070 --> 00:07:45,100
There are leaks in several places.

89
00:07:45,870 --> 00:07:46,900
You really need to take care of this.

90
00:07:47,510 --> 00:07:48,780
Otherwise, it'll be hard to rent out.

91
00:07:49,070 --> 00:07:51,810
Can I ask who lives here?

92
00:07:53,190 --> 00:07:54,810
A man moved in a couple of days ago.

93
00:07:54,830 --> 00:07:55,730
Just one guy.

94
00:07:56,430 --> 00:07:58,000
He moved in right after the last tenant left.

95
00:08:02,180 --> 00:08:02,880
I'll talk to him.

96
00:08:13,580 --> 00:08:16,740
[Yang Zhao]

97
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:12,020
What a coincidence.

98
00:09:13,230 --> 00:09:14,210
Is it?

99
00:09:15,630 --> 00:09:16,470
You showed up that day

100
00:09:16,470 --> 00:09:18,260
in the alley by the old mansion.

101
00:09:18,510 --> 00:09:20,180
And now we run into each other here.

102
00:09:21,400 --> 00:09:22,970
That's quite a coincidence.

103
00:09:26,230 --> 00:09:28,850
I... I wanted to explain in person.

104
00:09:29,160 --> 00:09:31,020
I went back to the old mansion to find you,

105
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:32,380
but you'd already moved out.

106
00:09:32,560 --> 00:09:33,490
You came looking for me?

107
00:09:37,400 --> 00:09:38,180
Thank you.

108
00:09:40,680 --> 00:09:42,180
I got the painting back from the hospital.

109
00:09:42,960 --> 00:09:44,450
You sure disappeared fast, though.

110
00:09:45,750 --> 00:09:46,940
You said you wanted to explain.

111
00:09:46,960 --> 00:09:47,970
So go ahead. I'm listening.

112
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:54,810
Do we really have to talk here?

113
00:09:54,980 --> 00:09:57,110
[Binjiang Police Station]

114
00:09:57,110 --> 00:09:58,060
Why not?

115
00:09:58,590 --> 00:10:00,810
The police are investigating the fire at the old mansion.

116
00:10:01,510 --> 00:10:02,850
They think someone may have set it deliberately.

117
00:10:02,870 --> 00:10:03,970
I have to cooperate with their investigation.

118
00:10:04,680 --> 00:10:06,020
If you won't tell me what happened,

119
00:10:06,680 --> 00:10:08,260
you can go inside and tell the police.

120
00:10:12,800 --> 00:10:15,940
The people who followed me that day were connected to you, weren't they?

121
00:10:17,350 --> 00:10:18,140
Yes.

122
00:10:19,040 --> 00:10:20,540
We do some business together.

123
00:10:21,830 --> 00:10:22,690
But Ms. Yang,

124
00:10:23,320 --> 00:10:25,660
I'm nothing like them.

125
00:10:27,510 --> 00:10:28,780
How are you different?

126
00:10:33,510 --> 00:10:34,420
I don't want to lie to you.

127
00:10:35,350 --> 00:10:37,260
So can I just not answer that?

128
00:10:38,990 --> 00:10:41,140
So you haven't been honest with me this whole time?

129
00:10:46,040 --> 00:10:46,780
Fine.

130
00:10:47,680 --> 00:10:48,660
If you won't tell me,

131
00:10:49,810 --> 00:10:50,900
we'll go our separate ways.

132
00:10:59,940 --> 00:11:03,620
[Yihai Dance Hall]

133
00:11:10,830 --> 00:11:11,610
Ladies get in free.

134
00:11:28,560 --> 00:11:30,300
Hey, beautiful. Can I buy you a drink?

135
00:11:30,350 --> 00:11:31,260
I don't drink.

136
00:11:32,630 --> 00:11:33,690
Then how about a dance?

137
00:11:33,710 --> 00:11:34,490
I don't dance.

138
00:11:34,830 --> 00:11:35,420
Sorry.

139
00:11:38,870 --> 00:11:40,140
Why come here if you don't drink?

140
00:11:41,830 --> 00:11:42,630
Just to avoid me?

141
00:11:44,080 --> 00:11:44,660
Avoid you?

142
00:11:45,920 --> 00:11:46,900
Don't flatter yourself.

143
00:11:47,560 --> 00:11:49,060
I'm not big on crowds,

144
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:50,300
but I do like

145
00:11:50,320 --> 00:11:51,730
trying new things.

146
00:11:52,400 --> 00:11:54,420
I heard this dance hall in Nanhu is famous.

147
00:11:54,440 --> 00:11:55,660
I've been wanting to check it out.

148
00:11:58,470 --> 00:11:59,450
What are they doing?

149
00:12:02,800 --> 00:12:03,940
It's called partner scouting.

150
00:12:04,960 --> 00:12:06,330
You can look around and pick

151
00:12:06,350 --> 00:12:07,970
a different dance partner for each song.

152
00:12:13,400 --> 00:12:14,780
Do you know the rules around here?

153
00:12:15,560 --> 00:12:16,610
This place has rules?

154
00:12:18,200 --> 00:12:19,810
If you want to dance with someone,

155
00:12:19,830 --> 00:12:20,780
you don't have to ask.

156
00:12:21,160 --> 00:12:22,380
Just give them a tap.

157
00:12:23,160 --> 00:12:24,060
If they're interested,

158
00:12:24,080 --> 00:12:25,090
they'll tap you back.

159
00:12:25,510 --> 00:12:27,090
Then you dance together on the next song.

160
00:12:32,680 --> 00:12:33,420
What are you doing?

161
00:12:34,980 --> 00:12:41,460
♪One day, I'll gracefully drift past you♪

162
00:12:43,620 --> 00:12:50,900
♪Oh, dream weaver, you broken soul...♪

163
00:12:50,920 --> 00:12:51,690
So,

164
00:12:52,560 --> 00:12:54,260
this place is basically a nightclub?

165
00:12:56,870 --> 00:12:57,660
Not really.

166
00:12:58,680 --> 00:13:01,490
A nightclub can cost thousands, even tens of thousands.

167
00:13:01,920 --> 00:13:03,210
Here, it's only 30

168
00:13:03,230 --> 00:13:04,140
to dance all night.

169
00:13:05,990 --> 00:13:07,730
You sure know this place well.

170
00:13:08,590 --> 00:13:09,420
Come here often?

171
00:13:11,990 --> 00:13:13,090
Let me guess. You don't want to lie to me again.

172
00:13:15,200 --> 00:13:16,900
So men can scout out women,

173
00:13:17,800 --> 00:13:19,570
and women can scout out men too, right?

174
00:13:22,380 --> 00:13:26,500
♪Two drifters...♪

175
00:13:28,350 --> 00:13:30,450
So who do you have your eye on?

176
00:13:31,100 --> 00:13:34,900
♪There's such♪

177
00:13:34,900 --> 00:13:37,780
♪a lot of world to see♪

178
00:13:39,780 --> 00:13:46,420
♪We're after♪

179
00:13:46,980 --> 00:13:51,860
♪the same rainbow's end♪

180
00:13:53,700 --> 00:13:55,100
♪Waiting♪

181
00:13:55,260 --> 00:13:57,420
♪'round the bend♪

182
00:13:57,540 --> 00:14:01,620
♪My huckleberry friend♪

183
00:14:02,060 --> 00:14:11,820
♪Moon River and me♪

184
00:14:36,630 --> 00:14:37,420
What's your problem?

185
00:14:38,040 --> 00:14:39,020
Are you deaf?

186
00:14:39,080 --> 00:14:40,490
The music stopped, and you stepped on my foot!

187
00:14:41,560 --> 00:14:42,570
Can't you hear or speak?

188
00:14:44,350 --> 00:14:44,850
Let's go.

189
00:14:45,280 --> 00:14:46,570
These are designer leather shoes!

190
00:14:46,630 --> 00:14:48,020
You got them dirty! You owe me money!

191
00:14:48,510 --> 00:14:49,090
Pay up!

192
00:14:49,750 --> 00:14:50,610
Give me my money!

193
00:14:50,830 --> 00:14:51,490
These people are scammers!

194
00:14:51,510 --> 00:14:52,060
Pay up!

195
00:14:52,680 --> 00:14:53,540
Where's my money?

196
00:14:53,990 --> 00:14:55,090
Want me to slap you?

197
00:14:55,230 --> 00:14:55,940
I'll beat you...

198
00:14:59,320 --> 00:15:00,090
Who are you?

199
00:15:00,830 --> 00:15:01,850
Take your fight outside.

200
00:15:02,630 --> 00:15:03,210
Let go!

201
00:15:03,920 --> 00:15:04,780
Stay out of this!

202
00:15:08,160 --> 00:15:09,490
Ow! That hurts! Stop!

203
00:15:12,960 --> 00:15:14,900
You're a grown man picking on a girl.

204
00:15:15,800 --> 00:15:16,570
Aren't you ashamed?

205
00:15:19,830 --> 00:15:21,380
Nobody's leaving tonight.

206
00:15:29,990 --> 00:15:31,020
How much does she owe you?

207
00:15:31,110 --> 00:15:31,900
I'll pay.

208
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:33,380
So you're with them, huh?

209
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:35,810
You let my dance partner get away.

210
00:15:36,320 --> 00:15:38,610
Now let your girl dance with me,

211
00:15:38,960 --> 00:15:40,450
and we'll call it even.

212
00:15:44,990 --> 00:15:45,900
Get him!

213
00:15:45,920 --> 00:15:46,570
Come on! Get him!

214
00:16:11,980 --> 00:16:16,820
[Yihai Dance Hall]

215
00:16:37,510 --> 00:16:39,180
Was that girl deaf?

216
00:16:40,830 --> 00:16:41,730
I think so.

217
00:16:42,200 --> 00:16:43,570
Sometimes they can't hear the music,

218
00:16:43,590 --> 00:16:45,260
so they lose track of how many songs they've danced.

219
00:16:45,280 --> 00:16:46,610
Then they argue with customers over payment.

220
00:16:47,610 --> 00:16:48,230
But sometimes,

221
00:16:48,230 --> 00:16:50,210
they use their hearing loss to make extra money.

222
00:16:50,800 --> 00:16:51,690
Who knows?

223
00:16:54,960 --> 00:16:56,300
Then why did you help her?

224
00:16:56,990 --> 00:16:59,260
I just can't stand seeing men bully women.

225
00:17:10,710 --> 00:17:12,860
Nobody's bothered you these past few days, right?

226
00:17:14,360 --> 00:17:15,140
No.

227
00:17:15,470 --> 00:17:16,250
Good.

228
00:17:18,750 --> 00:17:20,690
I'll take you home later, Ms. Yang.

229
00:17:22,790 --> 00:17:25,450
Could you stop calling me Ms. Yang?

230
00:17:27,840 --> 00:17:29,290
What should I call you, then?

231
00:17:31,070 --> 00:17:31,900
Ms. Yang?

232
00:17:33,050 --> 00:17:33,870
Teacher Yang?

233
00:17:36,070 --> 00:17:37,180
Just call me Yang Zhao.

234
00:17:40,230 --> 00:17:41,010
Okay.

235
00:17:41,960 --> 00:17:42,940
Yang Zhao.

236
00:17:50,750 --> 00:17:52,160
We should grab dinner sometime.

237
00:17:54,920 --> 00:17:55,420
Sure.

238
00:17:57,270 --> 00:17:57,830
Yang Zhao.

239
00:18:16,200 --> 00:18:17,210
We're here.

240
00:18:21,470 --> 00:18:22,490
Well, I guess...

241
00:18:24,790 --> 00:18:25,280
I'll get going.

242
00:18:27,760 --> 00:18:28,690
Where are you going?

243
00:18:32,360 --> 00:18:33,620
Aren't you home already?

244
00:18:57,460 --> 00:19:01,460
[Jiang Ming: Are you asleep?]

245
00:19:03,100 --> 00:19:11,500
[Jiang Ming: Are you asleep?]

246
00:19:11,500 --> 00:19:23,740
[Yang Zhao: Is your offer still good?]

247
00:19:23,740 --> 00:19:29,860
[What offer?]

248
00:19:41,200 --> 00:19:41,670
Hello?

249
00:19:42,960 --> 00:19:43,690
I said

250
00:19:44,550 --> 00:19:46,290
we should grab a meal sometime.

251
00:19:47,600 --> 00:19:48,450
Sure.

252
00:19:51,510 --> 00:19:52,860
You can cook, right?

253
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:55,420
How'd you know?

254
00:19:56,680 --> 00:19:57,690
I could smell your cooking.

255
00:20:01,750 --> 00:20:02,580
So...

256
00:20:03,600 --> 00:20:04,770
What would you like to eat?

257
00:20:09,440 --> 00:20:10,820
How about breakfast?

258
00:20:36,260 --> 00:20:40,900
[Yang Zhao: Hey, good morning.]

259
00:20:40,900 --> 00:20:48,540
[Jiang Ming: Morning! Breakfast is almost ready.]

260
00:20:55,980 --> 00:20:58,340
[Jinxian Pottery Studio]

261
00:21:23,360 --> 00:21:23,940
Pass it to me!

262
00:21:23,960 --> 00:21:24,450
Catch!

263
00:21:27,470 --> 00:21:28,210
Mister!

264
00:21:28,600 --> 00:21:30,210
Kick the ball to me!

265
00:21:33,160 --> 00:21:33,770
Catch!

266
00:21:36,960 --> 00:21:37,620
Where'd the ball go?

267
00:21:37,790 --> 00:21:39,660
Wow, mister! You're amazing!

268
00:21:39,680 --> 00:21:40,940
You kicked it so far!

269
00:21:40,960 --> 00:21:41,770
That was awesome!

270
00:21:54,470 --> 00:21:55,250
Dongba script.

271
00:22:11,070 --> 00:22:12,100
Sorry.

272
00:22:12,470 --> 00:22:13,530
All I've got is instant noodles.

273
00:22:14,680 --> 00:22:15,530
What's wrong with instant noodles? They're delicious.

274
00:22:17,310 --> 00:22:18,660
So what's your specialty?

275
00:22:21,600 --> 00:22:22,580
Sweet and sour ribs, I guess.

276
00:22:23,310 --> 00:22:24,140
Who taught you?

277
00:22:24,790 --> 00:22:25,620
My mom.

278
00:22:26,840 --> 00:22:28,140
It was her specialty, too.

279
00:22:28,360 --> 00:22:29,340
My dad loved it.

280
00:22:33,440 --> 00:22:34,620
What else can you make?

281
00:22:39,070 --> 00:22:39,860
Braised chicken.

282
00:22:40,960 --> 00:22:41,860
Eggplant with ground pork.

283
00:22:42,120 --> 00:22:43,140
- Dry-fried green beans. - Hold on.

284
00:22:43,640 --> 00:22:44,580
What happened to your hand?

285
00:22:45,030 --> 00:22:45,820
It's nothing.

286
00:22:47,510 --> 00:22:49,290
I accidentally cut it on a piece of pottery.

287
00:22:50,510 --> 00:22:51,100
Just a second.

288
00:22:51,310 --> 00:22:52,050
Where are you going?

289
00:23:01,750 --> 00:23:02,380
Does it hurt?

290
00:23:02,920 --> 00:23:03,690
No.

291
00:23:18,310 --> 00:23:19,100
Here, let me.

292
00:23:30,400 --> 00:23:31,180
Cut this for me, please.

293
00:23:37,120 --> 00:23:38,300
All done. Thanks.

294
00:23:39,360 --> 00:23:41,210
You don't like my bandaging skills?

295
00:23:41,360 --> 00:23:42,010
No.

296
00:23:42,840 --> 00:23:44,250
This knot won't come undone so easily.

297
00:23:45,790 --> 00:23:47,250
You seem pretty experienced.

298
00:23:48,710 --> 00:23:50,210
You get hurt like this a lot?

299
00:23:53,790 --> 00:23:55,050
Don't want to talk about it?

300
00:23:56,160 --> 00:23:58,530
You don't want to talk, or...

301
00:23:59,070 --> 00:23:59,860
You can't?

302
00:24:02,920 --> 00:24:04,140
I'm just not used to it.

303
00:24:06,070 --> 00:24:07,420
I've never liked explaining myself.

304
00:24:08,360 --> 00:24:10,100
It doesn't solve anything anyway.

305
00:24:10,400 --> 00:24:11,940
And talking too much never helps.

306
00:24:11,960 --> 00:24:12,490
Right?

307
00:24:13,270 --> 00:24:15,290
So over time, I got used to keeping quiet.

308
00:24:16,200 --> 00:24:17,380
Have you always been like this?

309
00:24:17,920 --> 00:24:18,860
Not always.

310
00:24:19,840 --> 00:24:21,250
Sometimes I talk a lot.

311
00:24:21,750 --> 00:24:22,530
Like when?

312
00:24:22,750 --> 00:24:23,530
Like right now.

313
00:24:39,640 --> 00:24:40,450
Ms. Yang,

314
00:24:41,400 --> 00:24:42,970
I've already paid my tuition.

315
00:24:44,070 --> 00:24:45,580
When do my lessons start?

316
00:24:57,310 --> 00:24:58,580
Want to give it a try?

317
00:25:01,270 --> 00:25:02,050
How?

318
00:25:07,880 --> 00:25:08,860
Let me borrow your hand.

319
00:25:16,230 --> 00:25:17,010
Let's start.

320
00:25:25,400 --> 00:25:26,530
Just gently press it against the clay.

321
00:25:27,070 --> 00:25:27,940
I'll guide you.

322
00:25:35,960 --> 00:25:37,820
That's Dongba script on there, right?

323
00:25:41,550 --> 00:25:41,920
Yeah.

324
00:25:42,950 --> 00:25:43,820
This ancient coin

325
00:25:43,840 --> 00:25:45,890
was used by the Naxi people for divination.

326
00:25:47,070 --> 00:25:48,400
Whenever they faced a decision,

327
00:25:49,400 --> 00:25:51,660
they'd toss the coin to help them choose.

328
00:25:52,310 --> 00:25:53,490
Have you made your choice?

329
00:25:54,470 --> 00:25:55,250
I have.

330
00:25:56,960 --> 00:25:58,050
Aren't you going to open it?

331
00:25:58,070 --> 00:25:59,180
How else will you know what you chose?

332
00:26:03,840 --> 00:26:04,660
I already know.

333
00:26:10,400 --> 00:26:11,340
The Naxi people...

334
00:26:12,680 --> 00:26:14,250
They live at the foot of Yulong Snow Mountain.

335
00:26:15,360 --> 00:26:16,820
You've been to Yulong Snow Mountain too?

336
00:26:18,030 --> 00:26:18,820
Yeah.

337
00:26:19,790 --> 00:26:20,860
What year did you go?

338
00:26:23,990 --> 00:26:24,900
Seven years ago.

339
00:26:25,990 --> 00:26:27,380
Seven years ago?

340
00:26:28,550 --> 00:26:29,730
2004?

341
00:26:33,310 --> 00:26:35,180
I painted this sunrise

342
00:26:35,200 --> 00:26:36,690
over the golden peaks that summer.

343
00:26:37,960 --> 00:26:38,730
I know.

344
00:26:45,960 --> 00:26:46,820
I painted this.

345
00:26:47,750 --> 00:26:48,900
You painted it?

346
00:27:00,550 --> 00:27:02,380
When the fire broke out that day,

347
00:27:02,400 --> 00:27:03,970
you rushed inside without a second thought

348
00:27:04,550 --> 00:27:05,860
just to save that painting.

349
00:27:07,200 --> 00:27:08,010
Weren't you scared?

350
00:27:11,990 --> 00:27:12,860
Of course I was.

351
00:27:15,440 --> 00:27:17,140
But I figured I might get lucky.

352
00:27:18,680 --> 00:27:21,530
If I could run back in and save just one thing,

353
00:27:23,840 --> 00:27:24,660
it had to be that painting.

354
00:27:28,990 --> 00:27:30,420
Then why did you go back

355
00:27:30,820 --> 00:27:31,460
to save it?

356
00:27:36,440 --> 00:27:37,210
You once told me

357
00:27:39,600 --> 00:27:40,530
that wherever you went,

358
00:27:40,550 --> 00:27:42,340
you'd always take that painting with you.

359
00:27:43,640 --> 00:27:45,140
It was the first piece you'd ever restored.

360
00:27:51,360 --> 00:27:52,250
That year, I was

361
00:27:53,160 --> 00:27:54,180
21.

362
00:27:55,600 --> 00:27:57,290
After graduating, I didn't want to go home.

363
00:27:57,840 --> 00:27:59,100
But I didn't know what to do next.

364
00:28:00,160 --> 00:28:02,380
I'd heard that the place closest to the sky

365
00:28:02,840 --> 00:28:04,290
could show you the path you were meant to take.

366
00:28:04,990 --> 00:28:06,290
So I went to Yulong Snow Mountain.

367
00:28:08,710 --> 00:28:09,860
It was my first time

368
00:28:10,640 --> 00:28:13,180
traveling so far on my own.

369
00:28:15,750 --> 00:28:16,820
We're here!

370
00:28:16,840 --> 00:28:17,890
We've arrived.

371
00:28:19,990 --> 00:28:20,940
Make sure you have your things.

372
00:28:24,920 --> 00:28:25,810
Hey, open the trunk.

373
00:28:32,790 --> 00:28:34,490
Miss, we're here.

374
00:28:34,510 --> 00:28:35,140
Don't forget your things.

375
00:28:35,160 --> 00:28:35,660
Thank you.

376
00:28:35,840 --> 00:28:38,180
Excuse me, is that Yulong Snow Mountain?

377
00:28:38,550 --> 00:28:39,940
Yep, that's Yulong Snow Mountain.

378
00:28:40,230 --> 00:28:41,430
The place closest to the sky.

379
00:28:41,520 --> 00:28:42,410
Okay, thanks.

380
00:28:43,300 --> 00:28:45,010
- Beautiful. One more.
- All right, let's go.

381
00:28:45,060 --> 00:28:45,840
Okay, sure.

382
00:28:46,800 --> 00:28:47,190
That's it.

383
00:28:48,230 --> 00:28:49,250
Sorry, go ahead.

384
00:28:51,030 --> 00:28:52,690
Okay, let's try another pose.

385
00:28:53,710 --> 00:28:55,140
Looking good! Let's take another.

386
00:28:55,680 --> 00:28:56,530
Make sure I look good.

387
00:28:56,790 --> 00:28:57,340
Okay!

388
00:29:08,640 --> 00:29:09,450
What's wrong, young lady?

389
00:29:09,990 --> 00:29:11,140
Did you lose your wallet?

390
00:29:11,230 --> 00:29:11,730
I...

391
00:29:12,230 --> 00:29:12,860
I don't even know

392
00:29:12,880 --> 00:29:14,290
when my wallet went missing.

393
00:29:16,990 --> 00:29:18,660
First time traveling so far from home, huh?

394
00:29:19,310 --> 00:29:20,340
When your wallet went missing,

395
00:29:20,360 --> 00:29:21,340
you didn't even notice, did you?

396
00:29:22,100 --> 00:29:24,250
It was crowded. Maybe you left it on the bus.

397
00:29:27,120 --> 00:29:27,900
Listen, young lady.

398
00:29:28,750 --> 00:29:29,420
Stop looking.

399
00:29:29,750 --> 00:29:30,380
You're not going to find it.

400
00:29:31,880 --> 00:29:33,380
You don't have any money left?

401
00:29:33,600 --> 00:29:34,010
No.

402
00:29:34,030 --> 00:29:35,580
Then call your parents.

403
00:29:36,030 --> 00:29:37,820
They're overseas on vacation with my brother.

404
00:29:40,270 --> 00:29:41,690
Well, you already

405
00:29:41,690 --> 00:29:43,010
paid me a 300-yuan deposit.

406
00:29:43,310 --> 00:29:44,660
That'll cover a week's stay.

407
00:29:44,990 --> 00:29:46,290
Get in touch with someone you know, okay?

408
00:29:50,270 --> 00:29:51,010
Thank you.

409
00:29:51,440 --> 00:29:52,100
Don't mention it.

410
00:29:53,070 --> 00:29:53,730
Um...

411
00:29:54,070 --> 00:29:56,210
Could I leave my paintings here for you to sell?

412
00:29:56,750 --> 00:29:59,100
Sure. Already found yourself a job, huh?

413
00:30:08,440 --> 00:30:10,250
I spent those days painting wherever I went.

414
00:30:11,360 --> 00:30:12,140
Luckily,

415
00:30:12,600 --> 00:30:14,580
I was able to make a living from my paintings.

416
00:30:20,400 --> 00:30:21,420
It was during that time

417
00:30:22,160 --> 00:30:23,660
that I painted those sunlit golden peaks.

418
00:30:24,880 --> 00:30:25,940
I don't know why,

419
00:30:26,510 --> 00:30:27,530
but I had this feeling...

420
00:30:28,550 --> 00:30:29,730
It was like I'd taken that trip

421
00:30:30,550 --> 00:30:32,210
just to paint that picture.

422
00:30:33,640 --> 00:30:35,100
I put it up for sale at the shop

423
00:30:35,120 --> 00:30:36,490
because I needed money for rent.

424
00:30:37,200 --> 00:30:39,770
But deep down,

425
00:30:40,070 --> 00:30:41,250
I hoped no one would buy it.

426
00:30:41,840 --> 00:30:42,580
You're back.

427
00:30:46,400 --> 00:30:47,010
Ma'am.

428
00:30:48,030 --> 00:30:49,100
Where's my painting?

429
00:30:49,310 --> 00:30:49,970
Which one?

430
00:30:50,400 --> 00:30:51,420
The sunlit golden peaks.

431
00:30:52,360 --> 00:30:53,730
Oh, I was just about to tell you.

432
00:30:54,310 --> 00:30:56,250
Someone bought it this morning.

433
00:30:57,640 --> 00:30:58,210
Here.

434
00:30:59,070 --> 00:30:59,860
This much?

435
00:31:00,440 --> 00:31:01,770
Didn't you need the money?

436
00:31:02,120 --> 00:31:03,820
Isn't it great that it sold?

437
00:31:04,270 --> 00:31:05,380
Why the long face?

438
00:31:05,790 --> 00:31:06,820
Who bought it?

439
00:31:07,840 --> 00:31:08,860
We get tourists

440
00:31:09,070 --> 00:31:10,970
coming and going all the time.

441
00:31:10,990 --> 00:31:12,140
I didn't know the buyer.

442
00:31:12,710 --> 00:31:13,490
I can't remember.

443
00:31:16,160 --> 00:31:17,820
I'd been so eager

444
00:31:17,840 --> 00:31:19,620
to sell my paintings to pay for my travels.

445
00:31:20,960 --> 00:31:21,970
But at that moment,

446
00:31:23,070 --> 00:31:24,210
I wasn't happy at all.

447
00:31:25,840 --> 00:31:26,690
I felt like

448
00:31:27,840 --> 00:31:29,380
I'd lost something precious.

449
00:32:02,600 --> 00:32:04,290
I felt like that painting was just like me.

450
00:32:06,470 --> 00:32:07,940
I had no idea what it had been through.

451
00:32:09,160 --> 00:32:10,340
Or why

452
00:32:11,400 --> 00:32:12,580
the person who bought it

453
00:32:13,710 --> 00:32:14,970
had abandoned it there.

454
00:32:19,710 --> 00:32:20,910
I went to so many places,

455
00:32:20,910 --> 00:32:21,970
[Baoxiang Temple]
trying to get it restored.

456
00:33:15,440 --> 00:33:16,580
You're still here?

457
00:33:17,710 --> 00:33:20,140
So much of this mural is missing.

458
00:33:21,840 --> 00:33:23,530
There's no way to restore it completely, is there?

459
00:33:25,710 --> 00:33:28,970
Aren't the missing pieces part of its story, too?

460
00:33:29,990 --> 00:33:31,900
Why make it look brand-new?

461
00:33:32,840 --> 00:33:35,490
This temple is a century or two old.

462
00:33:35,920 --> 00:33:39,250
We don't restore it to make it look the way it once did.

463
00:33:40,160 --> 00:33:43,250
We restore it so people remember its story.

464
00:33:46,200 --> 00:33:47,490
Remember its story?

465
00:33:48,920 --> 00:33:51,010
As long as someone cares about it

466
00:33:51,880 --> 00:33:52,940
and remembers it,

467
00:33:54,510 --> 00:33:55,940
it'll never disappear.

468
00:34:00,030 --> 00:34:03,340
Could you teach me how to do this?

469
00:34:07,620 --> 00:34:09,820
[Spring Dawn Bird]

470
00:34:13,240 --> 00:34:15,170
I stayed with my mentor for three months.

471
00:34:16,030 --> 00:34:17,220
During that time,

472
00:34:17,560 --> 00:34:19,250
I felt like I hadn't learned much.

473
00:34:21,030 --> 00:34:21,820
I still didn't know

474
00:34:22,020 --> 00:34:24,180
where to begin restoring my painting.

475
00:34:31,800 --> 00:34:32,610
Zhao,

476
00:34:34,590 --> 00:34:35,740
your craft

477
00:34:36,920 --> 00:34:38,970
is a path to becoming who you're meant to be.

478
00:34:41,110 --> 00:34:43,970
It may seem like we're restoring these things,

479
00:34:45,240 --> 00:34:50,450
but really, they're the ones healing us.

480
00:35:04,590 --> 00:35:06,380
I finally understood what my mentor meant.

481
00:35:07,440 --> 00:35:08,380
That's when I realized

482
00:35:09,360 --> 00:35:12,010
the luckiest part of my trip to the mountains

483
00:35:12,880 --> 00:35:14,740
was that through restoration,

484
00:35:15,190 --> 00:35:18,010
I was finally able to release

485
00:35:18,150 --> 00:35:22,050
all the feelings I'd buried and refused to face.

486
00:35:23,990 --> 00:35:25,300
Good. Very good!

487
00:35:31,360 --> 00:35:34,610
That was my first step as an artifact conservator.

488
00:35:39,400 --> 00:35:41,280
When I got back, I applied to

489
00:35:41,280 --> 00:35:42,790
the Repin Academy of Fine Arts in Russia.

490
00:35:43,520 --> 00:35:44,930
I studied artifact conservation.

491
00:35:46,920 --> 00:35:48,650
Maybe the place closest to the sky

492
00:35:50,240 --> 00:35:52,450
really can change someone's destiny.

493
00:35:54,550 --> 00:35:55,820
I hated snow so much.

494
00:35:56,920 --> 00:35:58,450
Yet artifact conservation

495
00:35:59,360 --> 00:36:01,350
led me straight into a world of ice and snow.

496
00:36:16,990 --> 00:36:18,050
Can I ask you

497
00:36:18,960 --> 00:36:20,380
what you do for a living?

498
00:36:31,510 --> 00:36:32,300
Then...

499
00:36:34,240 --> 00:36:35,130
Are you a good person

500
00:36:36,550 --> 00:36:37,490
or a bad one?

501
00:36:42,670 --> 00:36:44,010
Do you know her?

502
00:36:45,190 --> 00:36:46,260
Chen Mingsheng.

503
00:36:47,110 --> 00:36:48,650
That's the day we've been waiting for.

504
00:37:15,190 --> 00:37:15,970
Yang Zhao.

505
00:37:19,470 --> 00:37:20,340
Could you...

506
00:37:25,550 --> 00:37:26,340
Wait a few days for me?

507
00:37:29,030 --> 00:37:30,130
When I come back,

508
00:37:33,720 --> 00:37:35,010
I'll tell you everything.

509
00:37:38,990 --> 00:37:39,820
Okay.

510
00:37:40,920 --> 00:37:41,860
I'll wait for you.

511
00:38:08,100 --> 00:38:10,580
♪Rain♪

512
00:38:10,820 --> 00:38:13,580
♪Falls on a sea of faces♪

513
00:38:15,780 --> 00:38:17,980
♪You♪

514
00:38:18,660 --> 00:38:21,700
♪Walk toward me, silhouetted against the light♪

515
00:38:23,220 --> 00:38:26,660
♪After countless days and nights of waiting♪

516
00:38:26,780 --> 00:38:28,940
♪My heart beats out♪

517
00:38:29,140 --> 00:38:31,300
♪A wild rhythm♪

518
00:38:31,460 --> 00:38:32,980
♪Here we are together again♪

519
00:38:33,260 --> 00:38:36,500
♪You came back for me♪

520
00:39:54,590 --> 00:39:55,220
Mr. Bai.

521
00:39:55,840 --> 00:39:57,170
This just came in.

522
00:39:57,360 --> 00:39:58,130
Okay.

523
00:40:09,620 --> 00:40:13,420
[Police Personnel File]

524
00:40:44,380 --> 00:40:46,420
♪I'm not ready yet♪

525
00:40:47,820 --> 00:40:49,940
♪My feelings keep building up♪

526
00:40:51,580 --> 00:40:56,700
♪How much courage does it take to question old beliefs?♪

527
00:40:58,620 --> 00:41:00,820
♪How absurd♪

528
00:41:01,860 --> 00:41:04,500
♪I keep pulling away♪

529
00:41:05,700 --> 00:41:08,060
♪Running away, burying who I am♪

530
00:41:08,140 --> 00:41:11,340
♪Lost in the darkness♪

531
00:41:13,740 --> 00:41:18,260
♪Waiting for gentle morning light to fill my window♪

532
00:41:18,300 --> 00:41:25,420
♪Letting time slowly heal my wounds♪

533
00:41:27,940 --> 00:41:32,740
♪My thoughts are a mess right now♪

534
00:41:33,420 --> 00:41:36,260
♪Lend me a little light♪

535
00:41:37,060 --> 00:41:40,500
♪Write it down, don't say a word♪

536
00:41:40,620 --> 00:41:46,780
♪I'm afraid your words will be too cold♪

537
00:41:46,820 --> 00:41:50,980
♪Tomorrow will still bring pain♪

538
00:41:51,180 --> 00:41:54,820
♪Hold back the storm for now♪

539
00:41:54,900 --> 00:42:01,020
♪So I can bravely face the battle ahead♪

540
00:42:02,060 --> 00:42:07,980
♪So I won't lose my way♪

541
00:42:09,260 --> 00:42:15,100
♪Stay with me until dawn♪

542
00:42:17,540 --> 00:42:18,140
♪Open your hands♪

543
00:42:18,380 --> 00:42:22,420
♪Waiting for gentle morning light to fill my window♪

544
00:42:22,820 --> 00:42:30,380
♪Letting time slowly heal my wounds♪

545
00:42:32,500 --> 00:42:37,380
♪I can't bear the weight of the truth♪

546
00:42:37,860 --> 00:42:40,980
♪Lend me a little light♪

547
00:42:41,500 --> 00:42:44,740
♪Write it down, don't say a word♪

548
00:42:45,140 --> 00:42:51,220
♪I'm afraid your words will be too cold♪

549
00:42:51,700 --> 00:42:55,500
♪Tomorrow will still bring pain♪

550
00:42:55,780 --> 00:42:59,300
♪Hold back the storm for now♪

551
00:42:59,420 --> 00:43:06,020
♪So I can bravely face the battle ahead♪

552
00:43:06,380 --> 00:43:12,300
♪So I won't lose my way♪

553
00:43:13,620 --> 00:43:19,180
♪Stay with me until dawn♪
